WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:02.870
I have to apologize to you today.

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:07.870
I made a mistake on a story, I got a story
wrong and I want to fix it today.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:11.190
Donald Trump has been floating the idea.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:17.400
Of cutting the employee side of the payroll
tax for the rest of the year as a way to get

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.520
more money in people's pockets.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.730
People earning under one hundred and thirty
eight thousand dollars per year.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:29.430
I have multiple times said I was supportive
of this idea because it is true that it would,

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:34.770
in the immediate, put money back in the pockets
of workers earning under one hundred and thirty

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.770
eight thousand dollars a year.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.750
But I was wrong to support it.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.750
I was wrong.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.090
And I'm going to explain why today.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.540
Now, for people who don't know why or what
the payroll taxes.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.100
If you are a normal W-2 employee, you're not.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.100
You don't work for yourself.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.370
You're not a small business owner.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.890
You just work somewhere like most people do.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:57.770
You and your employer share some taxes that
come off of your payroll.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:02.420
Up until you earn one hundred and thirty seven
thousand seven hundred dollars per year, once

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:06.030
you get to 1:37 seven per year, you no longer
pay these taxes.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:12.000
There are two taxes twelve point four percent
towards Social Security and 2.9 percent for

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Medicare.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.000
OK, it only is on the first one hundred and
thirty seven point seven thousand dollars

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.960
a year that you earn.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:22.880
That is a total twelve point four and 2.9.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.630
That's about fifteen point three percent.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.460
The worker pays half and the employer pays
half.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.200
So the fifteen point three percent is split.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.200
Seven point six.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.350
Five percent for you.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.990
Seven point six five percent for the employer.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:46.090
Trump's idea was let's suspend the employee
half seven point sixty five percent through

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.830
the end of the year.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:54.150
But you would have to pay for it when you
file your taxes in 2021 for this year.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.590
So it is not a cut.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.210
It is a tax holiday.

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:04.170
Now, initially I said, listen, I do like it
because it puts money directly back in the

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:09.170
hands of people earning under one hundred
and thirty eight thousand dollars a year.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.790
Right now, it is not a tax cut for the rich.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.409
And I thought it was a good idea.

00:02:13.409 --> 00:02:16.909
I was wrong to support it for three different
reasons.

00:02:16.909 --> 00:02:23.370
And most importantly, this is another way
to actually backhandedly weaken Social Security

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.579
and Medicare.

00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:26.599
And I want to go through each of these reasons
one by one.

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:27.599
So three parts here.

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:34.019
Number one, the people who are in the roughest
shape right now are the 35 ish million people

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:35.560
who lost their jobs.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:41.269
If you lost your job, you're not paying a
payroll tax because you don't have a job.

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:47.629
So 7.6, 5 percent tax holiday off the payroll
tax for people who aren't on any payroll is

00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:49.310
not useful at all.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:55.250
Second, the people who do have jobs are mostly
earning the same amount of money now.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:01.290
I'm not saying they wouldn't love not to pay
the 7.6 5 percent, but you've got 35 million

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.909
people that straight up lost their jobs.

00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:05.900
So to them, the payroll tax holiday doesn't
make a difference.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:12.370
Most people, fortunately for now, are still
working and have not seen a decrease in pay.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.359
Some people are still working, but have seen
a decrease in pay.

00:03:15.359 --> 00:03:16.590
But it is not that many people.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:22.379
The bulk of the workers right now have not
seen a decrease in pay or are completely unemployed

00:03:22.379 --> 00:03:25.120
and thus unaffected by a payroll tax holiday.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.420
And the number three.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:27.889
It is only a tax holiday.

00:03:27.889 --> 00:03:28.949
This is not a tax cut.

00:03:28.949 --> 00:03:33.030
If you weren't one hundred thousand dollars,
for example, in a year, that means in the

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:39.340
second half of the year you would expect to
earn about $50000 for now, saving seven point

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:43.150
six five percent puts thirty eight hundred
dollars back in your pocket.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:49.310
But it is only a tax holiday when you file
your taxes in 2021 and you punch in how much

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:54.489
you've paid for Social Security and Medicare,
Turbo Tax or whatever, your accountant, whoever

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:58.719
will spit out, hey, that thirty eight hundred
dollars you didn't pay in the second half

00:03:58.719 --> 00:04:00.090
of twenty twenty.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:04.089
You've got to pay it back in right now because
it was only a tax holiday.

00:04:04.089 --> 00:04:09.560
So doing this payroll tax cut would target
a relatively small group.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:15.029
It would deprive the government of $950 billion
in revenue through the end of the year.

00:04:15.029 --> 00:04:19.630
It would weaken social security and Medicare,
which could then open the door to dirty tricks

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:23.650
from people like Trump and Larry Kudlow and
others to say, hey, we've got to do something

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.070
with Social Security and Medicare.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:29.660
We don't have that much money because of the
tax holiday you put in place and you've still

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:33.850
got to pay it back next year so we can't let
them do it.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:37.160
I apologize that I was supportive of this
early on.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:42.660
Given everything we now know, I cannot in
good conscience support this.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:46.280
And I'm sorry that I suggested that it would
have been a good idea.

